; worldsdialog.eval — the worlds dialog (W8), driven through the calls its rows make.
;
; `worlds dialog open <name>` is ONE click on that row's Open. A SECOND one on
; the same row relaunches the game and ends the run, so this script never makes
; one: it checks the ARM, which is the half that can be wrong without anyone
; noticing, and leaves the relaunch to `-project`, the scenario path.
;
; The world it creates is removed by WorldTest's cleanup, not here.
logecho on
reset
; Refused in a level: the world screen is the one state that routes input to it.
worlds dialog
worldmap on
worlds dialog
; Three refusals, each with its own sentence — a name that filters to nothing,
; and (after the create) a duplicate.
worlds dialog create !!!
worlds dialog create wt_dlg
worlds dialog create wt_dlg
; The running world offers no Open, so a click on it arms nothing new.
worlds dialog open dungeon-demo
worlds dialog off
; Reopened: nothing armed carries over from the last time.
worlds dialog
worlds dialog open wt_dlg
worlds dialog off
